# The scaling of a ball with one-limb center by a positive power of two c, with the special states
# of a ball: ball_mul_pow2_1, then the fix-up of ball_scale_1_full (milestone2.md, "Scaling a ball
# by a power of two"; milestone1.md, "Ball kernels"). One ball operand, so q is rx itself; |cz| is
# named az, as in ball_scale_1_full. The whole line when the scaled center or radius overflows.
# finite_when (statement B4): the result is a finite ball when no member of the operand times c
# exceeds a quarter of the overflow threshold in magnitude, (|cx| + rx) c <= 2^(emax - 2).
# exact_when: a finite result under the conditions of the core is c X exactly.
kernel:        ball_mul_pow2_1_full
input:         stored cx
input:         stored rx
input:         c
output:        cw
output:        rw
value:         cx*c
requires:      ball cx rx
requires:      power_of_two c
ensures:       encloses cw rw x*c x=cx,rx finite_when=abs_le((abs(cx)+rx)*c,-2) exact_when=zero_or_abs_gt(cx*c,eta/(2*u));zero_or_abs_gt(rx*c,eta/(2*u))
min_precision: 2
source:        ball_mul_pow2_1, then the fix-up of the special states of a ball (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       core: as ball_mul_pow2_1; fix-up: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallPow2.v ball_mul_pow2_1_full_correct
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after explicit tests that the center and the radius are finite (f) and that the operand is not empty (e); B1 to B4 of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels", state what comes out

(cz, rz) = ball_mul_pow2_1(cx, rx, c)
e        = eq(rx, rx)
az       = abs(cz)
f1       = lt(az, const inf)
f2       = lt(rz, const inf)
f        = and(f1, f2)
c0       = select(f, cz, 0)
r        = select(f, rz, const inf)
cw       = select(e, c0, rx)
rw       = select(e, r, rx)
